    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this hardware does not report",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 49
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\nThe GB10 is an integrated Grace-Blackwell part. Its driver returns **N/A** for\n`memory.total`, `memory.used`, `memory.free`, `power.limit`, `clocks.mem`,\n`fan.speed`, memory temperature and ECC counters — so those panels do not\nexist here rather than showing zeros.\n\n* **GPU memory** → use *unified memory* on the Host dashboard. There is no\n  separate framebuffer to measure.\n* **Power headroom** → no limit is exposed, so percentage-of-cap cannot be shown.\n* **Combined power** is the sum of the two GPU rails, **not** wall-socket draw.\n\nDetails and the DCGM test that led here: `docs/MONITORING.md`.\n"
      }
    }
